# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the host test.
#
# A parked record is one flag that flips once, written under the module's mutex and read under the
# RCU read side. The two do not order each other and do not need to: the read answers "is this name
# taken", and either answer is one the caller can act on. The record itself is freed only after a
# grace period, so the read is never on freed memory.
race:shadow_block.inc
